It's on Trusted Reviews.

00:35:34.510 --> 00:35:38.144
And they focus a little aspects
of how this phone is received.

00:35:38.144 --> 00:35:40.060
And what I'm going to
do with that is actually

00:35:40.060 --> 00:35:43.690
use that product review in the
context of our Natural Language

00:35:43.690 --> 00:35:44.570
API.

00:35:44.570 --> 00:35:47.470
So Natural Language
API offers things

00:35:47.470 --> 00:35:49.060
like named entity recognition.

00:35:49.060 --> 00:35:52.720
It recognizes the most relevant
entities in a block of text.

00:35:52.720 --> 00:35:54.959
So it finds things like
around organization.

00:35:54.959 --> 00:35:56.125
It finds things like people.

00:35:56.125 --> 00:35:59.160
It finds things like consumer
goods out of the box.

00:35:59.160 --> 00:36:01.690
And most common
[? nouns ?] primarily where

00:36:01.690 --> 00:36:04.510
these entities are normally
linked to a URL on Wikipedia.

00:36:04.510 --> 00:36:07.060
So you find if it's an
entity that's in Wikipedia,

00:36:07.060 --> 00:36:10.210
most probably will pick it up
from a Natural Language API.

00:36:10.210 --> 00:36:13.480
So let me go ahead and
grab this piece of text.

00:36:19.090 --> 00:36:20.830
I hate doing a live
demo sometimes.

00:36:20.830 --> 00:36:23.560
Because I actually
had copied it,

00:36:23.560 --> 00:36:25.162
but then mechanical problems.

00:36:37.960 --> 00:36:39.860
So let's go to analyze it.

00:36:39.860 --> 00:36:41.810
So one of the
things that I wanted

00:36:41.810 --> 00:36:44.510
to show that is the
first thing it picks up

00:36:44.510 --> 00:36:47.030
is if you look at this
concept called salience,

00:36:47.030 --> 00:36:49.200
so first thing is, it's
scanned this article.

00:36:49.200 --> 00:36:51.116
And it's picked up that
this article is really

00:36:51.116 --> 00:36:52.250
about the Nexus 6P, right?

00:36:52.250 --> 00:36:53.610
That's the first thing you
really want to understand.

00:36:53.610 --> 00:36:55.193
Hey, you're going
to get a lot of text

00:36:55.193 --> 00:36:56.630
coming into your organization.

00:36:56.630 --> 00:36:57.840
What is this article about?

00:36:57.840 --> 00:36:59.720
So that's the first
thing it finds out about.

00:36:59.720 --> 00:37:01.010
The other thing you
want to think about

00:37:01.010 --> 00:37:02.343
is things that's really focused.

00:37:02.343 --> 00:37:06.099
One of the key value points
that Google really want to land

00:37:06.099 --> 00:37:06.890
was premium, right?

00:37:06.890 --> 00:37:09.560
That's really, we
focus on Nexus 6P

00:37:09.560 --> 00:37:12.844
as a premium consumer
mobile device.

00:37:12.844 --> 00:37:15.260
And again, the good thing is
this article actually brought

00:37:15.260 --> 00:37:16.850
that up into [INAUDIBLE] flow.

00:37:16.850 --> 00:37:21.070
The other aspects we wanted
to talk about is, are there

00:37:21.070 --> 00:37:24.680
are pieces around design,
salience, other pieces that--

00:37:24.680 --> 00:37:27.650
are there other consumer
goods that's normally

00:37:27.650 --> 00:37:30.084
referred to with the Nexus 6P?

00:37:30.084 --> 00:37:32.000
In this case, for example,
we pick up the fact

00:37:32.000 --> 00:37:34.690
that people also talk
about Samsung Galaxy

00:37:34.690 --> 00:37:36.440
S7 in the same article.

00:37:36.440 --> 00:37:39.630
So you can imagine those are
substitutes from a customer

00:37:39.630 --> 00:37:40.130
perspective.

00:37:40.130 --> 00:37:43.320
We think about, how do we bring
those two products together?

00:37:43.320 --> 00:37:46.690
Let me do another example.

00:37:46.690 --> 00:38:05.211
In this case, I
brought up the Pixel C.

00:38:05.211 --> 00:38:07.627
So I'm going to go ahead and
copy that piece of text here.

00:38:18.530 --> 00:38:20.710
So in this piece,
again, the key pieces

00:38:20.710 --> 00:38:23.280
that you want to
think about is, so

00:38:23.280 --> 00:38:24.530
what do we want to understand?

00:38:24.530 --> 00:38:26.669
We want to understand what
is this article about?

00:38:26.669 --> 00:38:28.085
Second thing we
want to understand

00:38:28.085 --> 00:38:30.575
is, what other
organizations normally

00:38:30.575 --> 00:38:33.980
is referred to when we
talk about this product?

00:38:33.980 --> 00:38:35.870
We bring up aspects,
like Samsung.

00:38:35.870 --> 00:38:37.954
We think about other
products that goes with that.

00:38:37.954 --> 00:38:39.453
And then the other
thing that I want

00:38:39.453 --> 00:38:41.820
to also start thinking about
is, is this about a tablet?

00:38:41.820 --> 00:38:43.970
We figure out it's a
consumer good out of the box.

00:38:43.970 --> 00:38:45.470
You can imagine,
we start picking up

00:38:45.470 --> 00:38:47.310
salient entities out of this.

00:38:47.310 --> 00:38:49.240
So the piece that I
also want to then drive

00:38:49.240 --> 00:38:51.290
is, the next piece I
want to talk about is,

00:38:51.290 --> 00:38:54.020
how do we think about the
sentiment of this article?

00:38:54.020 --> 00:38:59.040
So I'm going to bring up an
article about Google Home.

00:39:17.190 --> 00:39:18.390
Sorry.

00:39:18.390 --> 00:39:21.972
I know watching me copy text is
not the most fun thing to do.

00:39:39.684 --> 00:39:40.960
So a couple of things.

00:39:40.960 --> 00:39:46.059
In this case, what we've done is
look at the sentiment analysis

00:39:46.059 --> 00:39:47.350
using our Natural Language API.

00:39:47.350 --> 00:39:49.630
So basically,
Natural Language API,

00:39:49.630 --> 00:39:52.960
when you take a block of text,
you run it through ML API,

00:39:52.960 --> 00:39:54.460
you get two kinds
of scores on that.

00:39:54.460 --> 00:39:55.690
You get a document sentiment.

00:39:55.690 --> 00:39:58.150
And the two pieces you
get is whether the score

00:39:58.150 --> 00:40:00.640
from minus 1 to plus 1.

00:40:00.640 --> 00:40:01.690
Minus 1 being negative.

00:40:01.690 --> 00:40:03.200
Plus one being positive.

00:40:03.200 --> 00:40:05.525
And then a magnitude of how
positive that article was.

00:40:05.525 --> 00:40:07.900
So in this case, you would
think this article is actually

00:40:07.900 --> 00:40:10.320
moderately pretty positive.

00:40:10.320 --> 00:40:13.210
And then it gives you things
like document sentiment.

00:40:13.210 --> 00:40:15.290
It kind of walks you
through how the article

00:40:15.290 --> 00:40:16.540
itself kind of flows.

00:40:16.540 --> 00:40:18.779
So as you guys start
thinking about taking

00:40:18.779 --> 00:40:21.320
this block of text, if you think
about product reviews coming

00:40:21.320 --> 00:40:23.710
in, you want to start
scanning all these articles,

00:40:23.710 --> 00:40:27.094
start figuring out which
article refers to my product.

00:40:27.094 --> 00:40:28.510
And then the second
thing you want

00:40:28.510 --> 00:40:30.610
to start thinking about
is, are these articles

00:40:30.610 --> 00:40:33.100
positive or negative
on my product?

00:40:33.100 --> 00:40:35.056
And the third part that
I'm not covering today

00:40:35.056 --> 00:40:36.430
is, you can also
imagine that you

00:40:36.430 --> 00:40:38.787
want to start looking at
which features are positive

00:40:38.787 --> 00:40:40.120
and which features are negative.

00:40:40.120 --> 00:40:42.036
And that's some part
we're not going to cover.

00:40:42.036 --> 00:40:45.305
So in the end, what
can you do with that?

00:40:45.305 --> 00:40:47.680
So you can imagine things like
relationship graph, right?

00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:52.140
So we've done is we
basically ran every Wikipedia

00:40:52.140 --> 00:40:55.030
article through our
named entity recognition.

00:40:55.030 --> 00:40:57.340
And we basically started
mapping a relationship graph

00:40:57.340 --> 00:41:00.460
based on which entities are
common together in an article.

00:41:00.460 --> 00:41:03.100
So this line
basically shows there

00:41:03.100 --> 00:41:06.764
are a lot of articles where, for
example, Nexus 6P and Motorola

00:41:06.764 --> 00:41:07.930
show up in the same article.

00:41:07.930 --> 00:41:10.030
It's a ticker line and
it's a shorter line.

00:41:10.030 --> 00:41:12.610
And the case, for example,
Nexus 6P and Sony, [INAUDIBLE]

00:41:12.610 --> 00:41:15.100
a few articles with the right
level things, a much longer

00:41:15.100 --> 00:41:16.480
line and it's a thinner line.

00:41:16.480 --> 00:41:20.770
So it's kind of a very crude
form of a relationship graph.

00:41:20.770 --> 00:41:24.130
So you can now thinking about,
how do all these products fit

00:41:24.130 --> 00:41:24.940
together?

00:41:24.940 --> 00:41:26.662
What's the relationship
with the product?

00:41:26.662 --> 00:41:28.120
You can even imagine,
you can start

00:41:28.120 --> 00:41:29.664
adding sentiment to that line.

00:41:29.664 --> 00:41:31.372
Say that this sentiment
is, normally, you

00:41:31.372 --> 00:41:34.132
got strong sentiments, positive
sentiments based on reviews.

00:41:34.132 --> 00:41:35.590
So you can get a
better feel as you

00:41:35.590 --> 00:41:38.140
start looking from a
product perspective,

00:41:38.140 --> 00:41:40.750
from the sales perspective,
how the relationships drive

00:41:40.750 --> 00:41:42.196
certain behavior.

00:41:42.196 --> 00:41:43.330
Does it make sense?

00:41:43.330 --> 00:41:45.834
And of course, that's great
from a product perspective.

00:41:45.834 --> 00:41:47.500
But what I want to
end with is something

00:41:47.500 --> 00:41:49.850
that's more important,
something for-- who

00:41:49.850 --> 00:41:52.004
is Tywin Lannister related
to in "Game of Thrones?"

00:41:52.004 --> 00:41:53.670
Because I'm a big
"Game of Thrones" fan.

00:41:53.670 --> 00:41:55.784
So you can imagine, you
can do something similar

00:41:55.784 --> 00:41:56.950
for "Game of Thrones" thing.

00:41:56.950 --> 00:41:59.680
And you can see right now the
Tywin Lannister is connected

00:41:59.680 --> 00:42:02.080
to Tyrion Lannister,
even though it should be

00:42:02.080 --> 00:42:04.290
a much stronger relationship.

00:42:04.290 --> 00:42:06.850
How many of you are
"Game of Thrones" fans?

00:42:06.850 --> 00:42:07.500
Not that many.

00:42:07.500 --> 00:42:09.560
So this joke just went
right over your head.

00:42:12.910 --> 00:42:14.960
So coming back.

00:42:14.960 --> 00:42:15.660
Slides, please.

00:42:18.890 --> 00:42:20.680
So what we went
through right now

00:42:20.680 --> 00:42:22.870
is, again, circling back
to what we talked about.

00:42:22.870 --> 00:42:25.065
We talked about the
three key scenarios

00:42:25.065 --> 00:42:26.440
that machine
learning can enable.

00:42:26.440 --> 00:42:29.790
One is, how do we find
the right product, right?

00:42:29.790 --> 00:42:32.290
How do we provide a more
intelligent search process

00:42:32.290 --> 00:42:33.760
